WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.830
- As a singer,

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.970
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.020
- If somebody said to me,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.450
and you know, I don't
mind who I admit it to,

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.800
if somebody said you could never act again

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.990
or never sing again, there
would be no competition.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.964
Singing is in my bloodstream.

00:00:11.964 --> 00:00:12.797
- It's so freeing.

00:00:12.797 --> 00:00:14.400
- It's my catharsis.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.040
It's in my soul and I miss it terribly,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.058
but this show-

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:18.891
- [Kelly] But you sing-

00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:19.800
- seems to like getting me to do both.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.614
- I know I was gonna say
you sing on Ted Lasso.

00:00:21.614 --> 00:00:22.447
- As football club owner.

00:00:22.447 --> 00:00:23.280
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.440
- I know, at the karaoke thing
and then the Christmas thing.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.910
Yeah. You've, you've sung on this show.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:27.743
- Yeah.

00:00:27.743 --> 00:00:28.576
- Sing, sang, sung, yeah.

00:00:28.576 --> 00:00:29.610
Sorry, mom.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.570
- Yeah. Sung.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.160
- Sure. And we all sing here.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.344
That's actually amazing.

00:00:33.344 --> 00:00:34.177
- I mean, kinda.

00:00:34.177 --> 00:00:35.850
I'm not singing on any
West End stages though.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.479
I'm not Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:38.910
- I'm not, I'm not singing
on West End either.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.210
- Nobody's Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.200
- So wait, is it, is it
true that "Ted Lasso"

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.430
is one of your dad's favorite things

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.263
that you've ever done?

00:00:45.263 --> 00:00:47.070
- Oh, my dad is very hard to please.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:48.360
He's very, very English.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.500
He's 81.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.960
He's just had quintuple bypass surgery

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.793
on his heart-

00:00:52.793 --> 00:00:53.626
- [Kelly] Oh no!

00:00:53.626 --> 00:00:56.760
- and he is just very unique.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.870
And lets me know when I'm in
something that he's not feeling

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.220
or that the people around-

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.410
This, he has watched three times,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.240
he's obsessed with the writing.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.073
- So good!

00:01:07.073 --> 00:01:09.630
- Right. Yeah. I mean, and
that for me is the litmus test.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:10.463
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:10.463 --> 00:01:11.296
- He's just-

00:01:11.296 --> 00:01:12.129
- [Kelly] It wasn't the fact

00:01:12.129 --> 00:01:13.363
that everyone loves it (laughing)?

00:01:13.363 --> 00:01:14.736
- [Hannah] Yeah. Yeah, it was probably.

00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:16.320
- [Kelly] It is the one
person we're always trying to

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.430
impress though that matters.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.380
So you really are a
football player, right?

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.530
- Yeah. Well, I mean I
used to play professionally

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.090
since I was a kid.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:24.923
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:01:24.923 --> 00:01:28.530
- Yeah, my grandma, when I started to walk

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.090
my grandma taught me how to play

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.809
in the garage of my house (laughing).

00:01:31.809 --> 00:01:34.860
I was always carrying a ball with me.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.693
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:01:35.693 --> 00:01:36.540
- And yeah, yeah.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.970
Football was part of me
and yeah since a kid,

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.340
then playing professionally when I was 15

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.083
and then later in life,

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:45.750
I stopped when I decided to study.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.080
And my parents told me to
study, and intelligently

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.880
because I had some injuries, but then

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.980
yeah, football it has
been part of my life.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.440
- So how did you land
the role on "Ted Lasso?"

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.821
Other than being perfect for it?

00:01:56.821 --> 00:01:57.654
(both laughing)

00:01:57.654 --> 00:01:58.770
- Well, thank you.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:02.460
I, well, I started my
Master in Acting in the UK.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.690
I saved money over there
and before going to the UK.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.410
And then I was in Mexico
and I received the audition

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.243
for Ted Lasso.

00:02:11.243 --> 00:02:12.630
I did it, didn't hear anything.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.770
They started shooting in August.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.050
So I thought, well, nothing happened.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.930
But then I received a random
tweet from Bill Lawrence,

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.127
show runner of the show, who said just,

00:02:21.127 --> 00:02:22.656
"Good audition, man."

00:02:22.656 --> 00:02:23.841
(Cristo laughing)

00:02:23.841 --> 00:02:24.674
- [Kelly] Really?

00:02:24.674 --> 00:02:26.070
- And I was like, okay,
either he's playing

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.239
with my feelings or there's something,

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:28.480
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:29.313
something good happening.

00:02:29.313 --> 00:02:30.146
- Oh My God, that'd be so mean.

00:02:30.146 --> 00:02:30.979
- [Cristo] Yeah.

00:02:30.979 --> 00:02:31.812
- [JoJo Siwa] So mean.

00:02:31.812 --> 00:02:35.580
- Yeah and then I did more
auditions and story short

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.860
I got the role for an Icelandic man.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.100
So when I arrived on
set, I was called Gunnar.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.500
And I was like, "If I'm
playing an Icelandic man,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.419
I need more preparation."

00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:46.290
- Wait, what?

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.570
So originally it wasn't even
the role you're in right now?

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.403
- No, no, no.

00:02:49.403 --> 00:02:51.570
The role was for a guy from Iceland,

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:55.200
but they liked my audition,
from what I know now.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.692
That they kept it and that's why they

00:02:58.692 --> 00:03:00.840
adapted it to who I am and-

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.218
- Oh My God, I love
that! You were so great.

00:03:03.218 --> 00:03:04.711
That's amazing!

00:03:04.711 --> 00:03:05.813
(audience clapping)

00:03:05.813 --> 00:03:08.610
- But are you getting
recognized everywhere?

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.820
- Well, yeah, here in LA,
this is where I realized

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.310
that a bit of the
craziness around the show

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.270
which I'm grateful and
stuff, yeah. Lots of fans.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.850
I have, I have a funny
anecdote that recently,

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.070
well I was in a commercial center.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:26.340
I went to the toilet and um, yeah.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.846
And then I was, I was
about to wee (laughing)-

00:03:29.846 --> 00:03:30.959
(audience laughing)

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:31.792
and then I just feel, I just feel someone

00:03:31.792 --> 00:03:34.440
staring at me and I'm like,

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.150
and then this guy very happy

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.960
and he just says, "Are you the
smiley guy from 'Ted Lasso'?"

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.310
Not even my character.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.257
And I'm like, "Uh, yeah."

00:03:43.257 --> 00:03:46.711
And he goes like, "Can I have a picture?"

00:03:46.711 --> 00:03:47.700
(Cristo and audience laughing)

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.440
- Can you, can you give me a minute?

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.077
- Not right now.

00:03:51.077 --> 00:03:51.990
- And I was like, um um okay-

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:52.997
- You're shaking (laughing).

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.667
- And then we got this selfie and he goes,

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:58.530
"Yes, thank you, man."

00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.827
And he leaves and I was like,

00:03:59.827 --> 00:04:00.903
"What the hell just happened?"

00:04:00.903 --> 00:04:01.736
(audience laughing)
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:04:01.736 --> 00:04:03.669
The show was nominated for a lot of Emmys.

00:04:03.669 --> 00:04:04.549
(audience applauding)

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:05.723
And you were also nominated
for an Imagen, right?

00:04:07.121 --> 00:04:07.954
- Yeah.

00:04:07.954 --> 00:04:08.787
- Imagen Award?

00:04:08.787 --> 00:04:09.620
- Yeah. Oh, thank you guys.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.310
Yeah, I'm very happy for the nominations

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.450
for the show in the Emmys.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.490
But yeah, we got this Imagen award.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.600
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.000
- Which awards Latin talent.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.290
And I'm just very grateful.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.190
And especially with the
people I'm nominated with

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.402
and I share the news with my family,

00:04:26.402 --> 00:04:30.360
and my family was more
excited with the fact

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.449
that I was nominated with
Mario Lopez (laughing).

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:35.138
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:04:35.138 --> 00:04:36.373
- Because I grew up, yeah, yeah-

00:04:36.373 --> 00:04:37.206
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:37.206 --> 00:04:38.160
- I love, I love that guy
- [Kelly] I love Mario.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.584
- I love him.

00:04:39.584 --> 00:04:41.707
And, and we love him
and I grew up watching

00:04:41.707 --> 00:04:42.570
"Saved by the Bell."

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.403
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:04:43.403 --> 00:04:44.236
- So my parents were like,

00:04:44.236 --> 00:04:45.268
"Oh my God, Mario Lopez!"
- I wanted to be in

00:04:45.268 --> 00:04:46.101
Zack Attack.

00:04:46.101 --> 00:04:47.220
Yeah, that's cool.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.050
- I wanted be in Zack Attack very much so.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.660
He was always cool. He made
that Speedo look very nice.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.493
- [Cristo] Yeah.

00:04:52.493 --> 00:04:55.376
- I freaking love Ted Lasso!

00:04:55.376 --> 00:04:56.209
- Ahhhhh.

00:04:56.209 --> 00:04:57.042
- I'm a nerd.

00:04:57.042 --> 00:05:00.360
Like I know everyone says
this, I'm not original.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.370
But it's just such a great show.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.190
It's so innovative and different
from all the other shows.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.710
And it's just a great, it's a good time.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.627
And I think, especially
for everybody, that's just

00:05:09.627 --> 00:05:12.750
felt trapped or maybe
having a (beep) year.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.010
I dunno if you could
say (beep) year on here,

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:14.970
but I just did.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:15.803
Anyway-

00:05:15.803 --> 00:05:16.636
- I mean, depends on the year,

00:05:16.636 --> 00:05:17.469
if the year was (beep) enough-

00:05:17.469 --> 00:05:18.302
- If it was-

00:05:18.302 --> 00:05:19.135
- you can say (beep) year.

00:05:19.135 --> 00:05:19.968
- you can label it.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.390
But um, no and it was just such a,

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.040
it's just such a great show.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.260
Like, I don't know one person
that doesn't like this show.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.940
How does that feel, to be part of such an

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.256
amazing show that everyone loves?

00:05:28.256 --> 00:05:30.089
(audience applauding)

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:31.502
Like, that's gotta feel cool.

00:05:31.502 --> 00:05:32.787
- Thank you.

00:05:32.787 --> 00:05:35.760
I mean, it's surprising and awesome.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:36.660
Like we-

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:37.920
- Is it surprising? Y'all didn't know?

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.753
You didn't think?

00:05:38.753 --> 00:05:39.586
- No, I mean, we thought, you know

00:05:39.586 --> 00:05:40.620
it was probably gonna be pretty good.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.510
There sure were a lot of
talented people involved,

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.940
but you know, we've all been fans of shows

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.042
that then got canceled for
reasons we don't understand.

00:05:47.042 --> 00:05:48.237
- Yeah.

00:05:48.237 --> 00:05:50.880
- And so we never could
have anticipated, you know

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.393
that I'd get to come here, first of all.

00:05:52.393 --> 00:05:53.445
- Yeah!

00:05:53.445 --> 00:05:54.278
(audience applauding)

00:05:54.278 --> 00:05:55.111
- [Brendan] It's great.

00:05:55.111 --> 00:05:56.610
- I would've never anticipated
it but I was very excited.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.340
Well, who inspired your
character, Coach Beard?

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.420
Did you have an inspiration?

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.994
- Ummm, several.

00:06:02.994 --> 00:06:04.740
- (laughing) You lucky man, you had

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.180
several people inspiring you.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.880
- I used to work as a stage hand

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.450
at my student union at
Illinois State University

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.160
in beautiful Normal, Illinois.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.273
The Bone Student Center, AKA the Boner.

00:06:17.273 --> 00:06:19.680
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.350
And the guys I worked with there,

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.150
you know who my bosses
were, just all these like

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.750
wonderfully laconic, very Midwestern,

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.060
but way smarter than they let on,

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.100
guys who were just very dry, very droll.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.330
And then they would just drop in a nugget

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.043
when it had had to be said.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.860
Like, I remember one
guy, he lost his radio

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:40.050
and just sitting there,
just all squat in the back

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:40.920
he lost his radio.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.970
Someone had stolen it or whatever.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.913
And he goes, "Oh no, my nomenclature."

00:06:44.913 --> 00:06:46.122
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:06:46.122 --> 00:06:47.370
Like nomenclature?

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.630
We're in Normal, Illinois.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.190
Who's saying nomenclature?

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.180
- Dropping that knowledge.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.740
- Yeah. So yeah, those guys.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.480
- I love, I love that.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.640
Well, you guys shoot in
London, I love London.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.050
Especially at Christmas time.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.873
What's the biggest cultural
difference for you?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.307
- Well one physical manifestation
that people make fun of

00:07:04.307 --> 00:07:07.590
but it's true, is every
time I cross the street,

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:08.520
I might die.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.290
Just, that never goes away.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.660
I've now spent a year of the
last two years of my life

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.780
in London, and every
day, several times a day,

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.380
I could die the most
awkward, embarrassing death

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.240
that I'll be known for forever.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.650
And I never ever get used to that.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.857
I have to at every
intersection be like (gasping),

00:07:26.405 --> 00:07:28.320
- Do they just not pay attention?

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.612
- Well, they're just
coming from the wrong way.

00:07:29.612 --> 00:07:31.645
(audience laughing)

00:07:31.645 --> 00:07:33.423
- Oh, well it's the right
way where they're at

00:07:33.423 --> 00:07:34.936
- But we know-

00:07:34.936 --> 00:07:38.340
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.183
- But is it?

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:42.690
So you became friends with your co-star,

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:43.950
Jason Sudeikis right?

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.950
Like was it, did y'all like
hit it off in Amsterdam?

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.030
Is this what I heard?

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:48.863
- [Brendan] Even before Amsterdam.

00:07:48.863 --> 00:07:50.610
- It's a place to become
friends with people, I think.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.460
- Isn't it? We knew each other in the

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:54.960
Chicago improv scene basically.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:55.793
- Oh, right on.

00:07:55.793 --> 00:07:57.570
- And then I moved to Amsterdam
to do comedy out there

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.120
and then he eventually followed and

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.730
that's when we became
like real solid friends.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.477
And that's where I
started telling him like,

00:08:04.477 --> 00:08:06.857
"Hey man, soccer doesn't
suck. Check it out."

00:08:06.857 --> 00:08:08.818
(Kelly laughing)

00:08:08.818 --> 00:08:09.973
And now it's our job.

00:08:09.973 --> 00:08:12.453
- (laughing) And it's the best job ever.

